//! Cold asynchronous operations and their completed outputs.

/// A runtime-local operation with one invariant output type `T`.
///
/// Creating a Future captures its inputs without starting work. The first
/// `.await` drives the operation and returns its output. Aliases share that
/// single-drive state, so awaiting the same Future again traps. Cancellation
/// terminates execution rather than wrapping the output in a `Result`.
///
/// There is no public constructor. Calling an `async fn` or evaluating an
/// `async` block creates a Future.
///
/// ```kagari
/// use core::future::Future;
///
/// async fn answer() -> i32 {
///     42
/// }
///
/// fn pending_answer() -> Future<i32> {
///     answer()
/// }
/// ```
pub native type Future<T>;
